            <ArticleTitle>Endometriosis resembling endometrial cancer in a postmenopausal patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/13697137.2017.1398229</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endometriosis occurs in 2-4% of postmenopausal women. There have been a few reports of endometriosis in women in whom neither history nor diagnostic imaging indicated the presence of this disease, either at reproductive age or after menopause. A case is described of an 84-year-old patient with extensive deep pelvic endometriosis imitating advanced neoplastic process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
